{{!-- A1's cover: the newest post at cover size — full-bleed over its photograph, type-set on the
page when it has none.

	{{> "home/hero" feed=feed}}

The lead is the first row of the shared query, which is to say the most recent post. That is the
signal, not a position in a fixture: the publication's own reverse-chronological order decides
what leads the cover, so publishing moves it.

THE PHOTOGRAPHED COVER, which is the one the design draws. `h-[min(76vh,660px)]` is the design's
height, and it is viewport-relative on purpose — worth knowing when reading a capture, since a
screenshot's window is as tall as the page, so 76vh always resolves past the 660px cap there. The
text colours are literal white rather than theme tokens, and the panel behind the photograph is
literal `#0c0a09`: the scrim is dark in both Modes, so nothing there can resolve against the
page. Those are the theme's only non-token colours and they are the same colour — rgb(12 10 9),
the darkest stop of the `hero-scrim` gradient in src/styles/main.css.

THE TYPE-SET COVER, which the design does not draw, because Ghost lets a post publish with no
image. It is not the photographed cover with the photograph missing: a dark 660px panel is a
place where a picture should be, and this band is instead a cover made of type — eyebrow, rule,
the title at display size, rule, the standfirst in italic — on the page's own background, closed
by one hairline. Every colour is a token, so it repaints in dark Mode like everything else, and
the band's height is its content rather than 76vh.

It replaces an accent wash and an isometric lattice over that dark panel, which is what this
branch drew until 2026-09 (docs/adr/0004, superseded in part by docs/adr/0005). The eyebrow
carries the primary tag where the post has one and the word "Latest" where it does not —
Handlebars runs a block's inverse on a falsy value, so `{{#primary_tag}}…{{else}}…{{/primary_tag}}`
is the whole of that. The tag is a link and the fallback is not, because a label that goes
nowhere should not look clickable.

`clamp(38px,5.4vw,112px)` is the photographed cover's own ramp with its 72px ceiling raised. The
cap is higher because a type-set cover has no photograph to share the band with, and it may be
raised at all because the design draws nothing here — this branch carries no Floor. --}}
{{#foreach feed limit="1"}}
	{{#if feature_image}}
		<section
			aria-labelledby="a1-lead"
			class="border-border relative border-b">
			<div class="relative h-[min(76vh,660px)] overflow-hidden bg-[#0c0a09]">
				<img
					src="{{img_url feature_image size="xxl"}}"
					{{#if feature_image_alt}}alt="{{feature_image_alt}}"{{else}}alt=""{{/if}}
					fetchpriority="high"
					decoding="async"
					class="block h-full w-full object-cover">

				<div
					aria-hidden="true"
					class="hero-scrim absolute inset-0"></div>

				<div class="absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 pb-14">
					<div class="container">
						<div class="flex items-center gap-3.5">
							{{#primary_tag}}
								<a
									href="{{url}}"
									class="font-meta tracking-meta border-b border-white/50 text-xs text-white uppercase no-underline">{{name}}</a>
							{{/primary_tag}}

							<span class="font-meta tracking-meta text-xs text-white/72 uppercase">{{> "dateline"}}</span>
						</div>

						<h1
							id="a1-lead"
							class="font-display tracking-display mt-[18px] max-w-[20ch] text-[clamp(38px,5.4vw,72px)] leading-[1.03] font-medium text-balance text-white">
							<a
								href="{{url}}"
								class="text-white no-underline">{{title}}</a>
						</h1>

						<p class="text-lead mt-5 max-w-[56ch] leading-[1.5] text-pretty text-white/82">{{excerpt}}</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	{{else}}
		<section
			aria-labelledby="a1-lead"
			class="border-border border-b">
			<div class="container pt-14 pb-16">
				{{!-- The rule under the eyebrow is this row's bottom border, NOT the h1's top border, and
				that is a measurement constraint rather than taste: the width audit counts a heading's
				lines as `round(height / lineHeight)` (scripts/verify/probe-audit.js), so 24px of
				padding plus a 1px rule on the h1 reads as 0.69 of an extra line and turns a genuine
				four-line title at 320px into a reported five — one over the limit. Keep the h1's box
				to its own text. --}}
				<div class="border-border flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3.5 border-b pb-[18px]">
					{{#primary_tag}}
						<a
							href="{{url}}"
							class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-accent border-accent/45 border-b uppercase no-underline">{{name}}</a>
					{{else}}
						<span class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-accent uppercase">{{t "Latest"}}</span>
					{{/primary_tag}}

					<span class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-muted uppercase">{{> "dateline"}}</span>
				</div>

				{{!-- `leading-[1]`, and the title's own `my-6` is the only space around it: the rules
				above and below belong to the eyebrow row and the standfirst, so one symmetric margin
				on the heading sets both gaps and there is nothing to keep in sync. Newsreader's
				content area is ~1.24em, so at leading 1 the last line's descenders hang a few px
				below the h1's own bottom edge — which is why the visible gap under the title always
				measures smaller than the number in the class, and why a 56px margin here read as 49px
				against 18px above. --}}
				{{!-- WHAT STAYS ON THE h1 AND WHY, because it looks arbitrary: the size, the leading and
				`text-balance`. The width audit counts a heading's lines as `round(height / lineHeight)`
				(scripts/verify/probe-audit.js) and Tailwind's preflight gives headings
				`font-size: inherit`, so type declared on the link leaves the h1 computing 16px/normal
				and a two-line title reports as eight. `text-balance` applies to the block that holds
				the lines, which is the h1 while the link is inline. Family, tracking, weight, colour
				and the decoration are the link's. --}}
				<h1
					id="a1-lead"
					class="my-6 text-[clamp(38px,5.4vw,112px)] leading-[1] text-balance">
					<a
						href="{{url}}"
						class="font-display tracking-display text-text font-medium no-underline">{{title}}</a>
				</h1>

				<p
					class="font-body text-lead text-muted border-border max-w-[66ch] border-t pt-5 leading-[1.55] text-pretty italic">{{excerpt}}</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	{{/if}}
{{/foreach}}
